+Each asynchronous call allocates its status with this resource. With a
+resource allocating managed memory, each call then allocates and frees
+managed memory, which is slow. A pool of the standard library over this
+resource avoids it:
+
+~~~~{.cxx}
+auto managed = mgis::memory_resources::CUDAManagedMemoryResource{};
+auto pool = std::pmr::synchronized_pool_resource(&managed);
+auto p = AsynchronousBatchExecutionPolicy{};
+p.resource = &pool;
+p.location = MemoryLocation::SHARED;
+~~~~
+
+With a pool, a pending computation destroyed before the computations are
+completed corrupts the next call instead of only being slow: the
+precondition below is all the more important. The rotation matrices built
+from material axes by an asynchronous rotation are also allocated by this
+resource: for repeated rotations, they shall rather be built once by
+`buildRotationMatrices`.
